<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38513" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεισ-έρχομαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>come in besides,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>
			<i>to</i> one, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				8.35
			</span></i>; esp. into a family as stepmother, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.154
			</span></i>; <i>rush in and attack,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεισήλθοσαν τῷ Σίμωνι εἰς τὸ
					συμπόσιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>1 Ma.</u>
					16.16
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>UPZ</u>
				13.19
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>come in after,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.37
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατόπιν τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Prt.</u>
					316a
				</span></i>
			; and freq. in 
				Att.
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Dem.</u>
					8
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>come into besides,</i> c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξένος ἐ. πόλιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					813
				</span></i>
			: c. dat., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόμοις</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				851
			</span></i> (nisi leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόμους</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; εἰς τὸ χωρίον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					47.53
				</span></i>
			; of things, <i>to be imported,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐκ πάσης γῆς τὰ πάντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.38
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> of customs, <i>to be
				introduced later,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.676f
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>come into</i> one's <i>head, occur to</i> one, c. dat., ib. <i><span class="en">
				585f
			</span></i>: c. acc., <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>VH</u>
				2.42
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
